[2026-03-14T19:28:12.375Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKSMZeMuvbJBPNHcEBrpFF","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile a comprehensive summary with all the findings:\n\n## Comprehensive Google Flights App Exploration Report\n\n### 1. App Directory Name and Structure\n\n**App Directory**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/`\n\n**Key Structure**:\n```\nGoogleFlights/\n├── src/\n│   ├── components/          (25+ React components)\n│   ├── pages/               (5 page components)\n│   ├── slices/              (5 Redux slices)\n│   ├── App.tsx\n│   ├── store.ts\n│   └── main.tsx\n├── netlify/functions/       (12 serverless functions)\n├── tests/                   (Empty - test files to be created)\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── test.ts\n│   ├── check.ts\n│   ├── deploy.ts\n│   └── schema.ts\n├── docs/tests.md            (Comprehensive test specifications)\n├── playwright.config.ts\n├── package.json\n├── vite.config.ts\n└── Other config files\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. TripTypeSelector Component Source Code\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripTypeSelector.tsx`\n\n```typescript\nimport { useState, useRef, useEffect } from 'react'\nimport { useDispatch, useSelector } from 'react-redux'\nimport { setTripType, type TripType } from '../slices/searchSlice'\nimport type { RootState } from '../store'\nimport './TripTypeSelector.css'\n\nconst tripTypes: { value: TripType; label: string }[] = [\n  { value: 'round_trip', label: 'Round trip' },\n  { value: 'one_way', label: 'One way' },\n  { value: 'multi_city', label: 'Multi-city' },\n]\n\nfunction TripTypeSelector() {\n  const dispatch = useDispatch()\n  const tripType = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.search.tripType)\n  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false)\n  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    function handleClickOutside(e: MouseEvent) {\n      if (ref.current && !ref.current.contains(e.target as Node)) {\n        setIsOpen(false)\n      }\n    }\n    if (isOpen) {\n      document.addEventListener('mousedown', handleClickOutside)\n      return () => document.removeEventListener('mousedown', handleClickOutside)\n    }\n  }, [isOpen])\n\n  const selectedLabel = tripTypes.find((t) => t.value === tripType)?.label || 'Round trip'\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"trip-type-selector\" ref={ref} data-testid=\"trip-type-selector\">\n      <button\n        className=\"trip-type-selector__trigger\"\n        onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}\n        data-testid=\"trip-type-selector-trigger\"\n      >\n        <span>{selectedLabel}</span>\n        <span className=\"trip-type-selector__arrow\">{isOpen ? '▲' : '▼'}</span>\n      </button>\n      {isOpen && (\n        <div className=\"trip-type-selector__dropdown\" data-testid=\"trip-type-selector-dropdown\">\n          {tripTypes.map((type) => (\n            <button\n              key={type.value}\n              className={`trip-type-selector__option ${tripType === type.value ? 'trip-type-selector__option--selected' : ''}`}\n              onClick={() => {\n                dispatch(setTripType(type.value))\n                setIsOpen(false)\n              }}\n              data-testid={`trip-type-option-${type.value}`}\n            >\n              {type.label}\n            </button>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport default TripTypeSelector\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Custom dropdown (not native select)\n- Three trip type options: Round trip, One way, Multi-city\n- Click-outside detection to close dropdown\n- Redux integration using `setTripType` action\n- Data-testid attributes for testing\n\n**CSS File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/TripTypeSelector.css`\n- Uses CSS custom properties for theming (--color-text-primary, --color-surface, etc.)\n- Dropdown positioning with z-index 100\n- Hover effects on trigger and options\n\n---\n\n### 3. CabinClassSelector Component Source Code\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CabinClassSelector.tsx`\n\n```typescript\nimport { useState, useRef, useEffect } from 'react'\nimport { useDispatch, useSelector } from 'react-redux'\nimport { setCabinClass, type CabinClass } from '../slices/searchSlice'\nimport type { RootState } from '../store'\nimport './CabinClassSelector.css'\n\nconst cabinClasses: { value: CabinClass; label: string }[] = [\n  { value: 'economy', label: 'Economy' },\n  { value: 'premium_economy', label: 'Premium Economy' },\n  { value: 'business', label: 'Business' },\n  { value: 'first', label: 'First' },\n]\n\nfunction CabinClassSelector() {\n  const dispatch = useDispatch()\n  const cabinClass = useSelector((state: RootState) => state.search.cabinClass)\n  const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false)\n  const ref = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null)\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    function handleClickOutside(e: MouseEvent) {\n      if (ref.current && !ref.current.contains(e.target as Node)) {\n        setIsOpen(false)\n      }\n    }\n    if (isOpen) {\n      document.addEventListener('mousedown', handleClickOutside)\n      return () => document.removeEventListener('mousedown', handleClickOutside)\n    }\n  }, [isOpen])\n\n  const selectedLabel = cabinClasses.find((c) => c.value === cabinClass)?.label || 'Economy'\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"cabin-class-selector\" ref={ref} data-testid=\"cabin-class-selector\">\n      <button\n        className=\"cabin-class-selector__trigger\"\n        onClick={() => setIsOpen(!isOpen)}\n        data-testid=\"cabin-class-trigger\"\n      >\n        <span>{selectedLabel}</span>\n        <span className=\"cabin-class-selector__arrow\">{isOpen ? '▲' : '▼'}</span>\n      </button>\n      {isOpen && (\n        <div className=\"cabin-class-selector__dropdown\" data-testid=\"cabin-class-dropdown\">\n          {cabinClasses.map((cls) => (\n            <button\n              key={cls.value}\n              className={`cabin-class-selector__option ${cabinClass === cls.value ? 'cabin-class-selector__option--selected' : ''}`}\n              onClick={() => {\n                dispatch(setCabinClass(cls.value))\n                setIsOpen(false)\n              }}\n              data-testid={`cabin-class-option-${cls.value}`}\n            >\n              {cls.label}\n            </button>\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      )}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n\nexport default CabinClassSelector\n```\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Four cabin class options: Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First\n- Same architecture as TripTypeSelector (custom dropdown with click-outside detection)\n- Redux integration using `setCabinClass` action\n- All options have data-testid attributes\n- Dropdown min-width: 180px (slightly wider than TripTypeSelector at 160px)\n\n**CSS File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/CabinClassSelector.css`\n- Nearly identical styling to TripTypeSelector\n- Same positioning and hover effects\n\n---\n\n### 4. Related Components\n\n**PassengerCountSelector** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/PassengerCountSelector.tsx`):\n- Similar dropdown structure but with increment/decrement buttons\n- Manages three categories: Adults, Children, Infants\n- Business logic for constraints (min 1 adult, infants ≤ adults)\n- Uses Redux `setPassengers` action\n\n---\n\n### 5. Redux State Management\n\n**searchSlice.ts** (`/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/searchSlice.ts`):\n\n**Type Definitions**:\n```typescript\nexport type TripType = 'round_trip' | 'one_way' | 'multi_city'\nexport type CabinClass = 'economy' | 'premium_economy' | 'business' | 'first'\n\ninterface SearchState {\n  tripType: TripType\n  passengers: {\n    adults: number\n    children: number\n    infants: number\n  }\n  cabinClass: CabinClass\n  origin: Airport | null\n  destination: Airport | null\n  departureDate: string | null\n  returnDate: string | null\n  recentSearches: RecentSearch[]\n  recentSearchesLoading: boolean\n  popularDestinations: PopularDestination[]\n  popularDestinationsLoading: boolean\n  sessionToken: string\n  validationErrors: Record<string, string>\n}\n```\n\n**Initial State**:\n```typescript\nconst initialState: SearchState = {\n  tripType: 'round_trip',\n  passengers: { adults: 1, children: 0, infants: 0 },\n  cabinClass: 'economy',\n  origin: null,\n  destination: null,\n  departureDate: null,\n  returnDate: null,\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n**Relevant Reducers**:\n- `setTripType`: Updates trip type, clears return date if switching to 'one_way'\n- `setCabinClass`: Updates cabin class\n- `setPassengers`: Updates all passenger counts\n\n---\n\n### 6. docs/tests.md File for Test Specifications\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` (94.6 KB - comprehensive test specification)\n\n**Coverage includes**:\n\n#### TripTypeSelector Tests (7 tests):\n1. Displays default \"Round trip\" selection\n2. Opens dropdown and shows all options\n3. Selects \"One way\" and hides return date\n4. Selects \"Multi-city\" option\n5. Switches back to \"Round trip\" from \"One way\"\n6. Closes dropdown when clicking outside\n7. Can be used multiple times in sequence\n\n#### CabinClassSelector Tests (7 tests):\n1. Displays default \"Economy\"\n2. Opens dropdown showing all cabin classes\n3. Selects \"Business\" class\n4. Selects \"Premium Economy\" class\n5. Selects \"First\" class\n6. Closes dropdown when clicking outside\n7. Can be changed multiple times\n\n#### PassengerCountSelector Tests (10 tests)\n#### AirportAutocomplete Tests (12 tests)\n#### DatePicker Tests (11 tests)\n#### SearchButton Tests (8 tests)\n#### RecentSearches Tests (6 tests)\n#### PopularDestinations Tests (5 tests)\n#### SearchResultsPage Components Tests (13+ tests)\n\n**Total**: 79+ test specifications covering all major functionality\n\n---\n\n### 7. Existing Test Files\n\n**Current Status**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/` is **EMPTY** - no test files exist yet.\n\n**Note**: There is one spec file in node_modules