elects \"Business\" class\n4. Selects \"Premium Economy\" class\n5. Selects \"First\" class\n6. Closes dropdown when clicking outside\n7. Can be changed multiple times\n\n#### PassengerCountSelector Tests (10 tests)\n#### AirportAutocomplete Tests (12 tests)\n#### DatePicker Tests (11 tests)\n#### SearchButton Tests (8 tests)\n#### RecentSearches Tests (6 tests)\n#### PopularDestinations Tests (5 tests)\n#### SearchResultsPage Components Tests (13+ tests)\n\n**Total**: 79+ test specifications covering all major functionality\n\n---\n\n### 7. Existing Test Files\n\n**Current Status**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/` is **EMPTY** - no test files exist yet.\n\n**Note**: There is one spec file in node_modules from @reduxjs/toolkit, but no application test files have been created.\n\n---\n\n### 8. playwright.config.ts Configuration\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test'\nimport { getExecutablePath } from '@replayio/playwright'\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  testDir: './tests',\n  timeout: 60000,\n  expect: { timeout: 10000 },\n  fullyParallel: false,\n  retries: 0,\n  workers: 1,\n  reporter: [['list'], ['json', { outputFile: 'test-results/results.json' }]],\n  use: {\n    baseURL: 'http://localhost:8888',\n    trace: 'on-first-retry',\n    launchOptions: {\n      executablePath: getExecutablePath('chromium'),\n    },\n  },\n  projects: [\n    {\n      name: 'replay-chromium',\n      use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },\n    },\n  ],\n  webServer: {\n    command: 'npx netlify dev --port 8888 --functions ./netlify/functions',\n    port: 8888,\n    reuseExistingServer: !process.env.CI,\n    timeout: 30000,\n  },\n})\n```\n\n**Key Configuration**:\n- Test directory: `./tests`\n- Timeout: 60 seconds per test\n- Parallel execution disabled (fullyParallel: false)\n- Single worker (workers: 1)\n- Reports: List + JSON output to `test-results/results.json`\n- Base URL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- Web server: Netlify dev on port 8888\n- Browser: Chromium via Replay.io for debugging\n\n---\n\n### 9. package.json Scripts\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/package.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"google-flights\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"vite\",\n    \"build\": \"vite build\",\n    \"preview\": \"vite preview\",\n    \"check\": \"tsx scripts/check.ts\",\n    \"test\": \"tsx scripts/test.ts\",\n    \"deploy\": \"tsx scripts/deploy.ts\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**Available Commands**:\n1. `npm run dev` - Start Vite dev server\n2. `npm run build` - Build production bundle\n3. `npm run preview` - Preview production build\n4. `npm run check` - Run checks\n5. `npm run test <test-file>` - Run Playwright tests (requires test file argument)\n6. `npm run deploy` - Deploy application\n\n**Test Execution**:\n- Uses `tsx` to run TypeScript test script\n- Test script (`scripts/test.ts`):\n  - Kills any stale processes\n  - Creates ephemeral Neon database branch\n  - Initializes and seeds database\n  - Starts Netlify dev server\n  - Runs Playwright tests with Replay.io recording\n  - Uploads failed test recordings automatically\n  - Cleans up test branch and local recordings\n\n---\n\n### 10. Dependencies\n\n**Key Dependencies**:\n- React 18.3.1\n- React Redux 9.2.0\n- Redux Toolkit 2.5.0\n- React Router DOM 7.1.1\n- Vite 6.0.5\n\n**Key Dev Dependencies**:\n- Playwright 1.49.1\n- Replay.io Playwright 5.0.0\n- TypeScript 5.7.2\n- ESLint 9.17.0\n\n---\n\n### 11. Component Usage in SearchPage\n\n**File**: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/pages/SearchPage.tsx`\n\nBoth TripTypeSelector and CabinClassSelector are used in the SearchPage along with PassengerCountSelector:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"search-page__selectors\">\n  <TripTypeSelector />\n  <PassengerCountSelector />\n  <CabinClassSelector />\n</div>\n```\n\nAll three selectors are positioned together at the top of the search form, followed by airport selection and date pickers.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThe Google Flights app is a fully-featured React application with:\n- **Redux state management** for all search parameters\n- **Custom dropdown components** with click-outside detection and keyboard navigation\n- **Comprehensive test specifications** in docs/tests.md covering 79+ test cases\n- **Empty tests directory** ready for Playwright test implementation\n- **Netlify serverless backend** with 12 functions\n- **Replay.io integration** for automatic test recording and debugging\n- **Database-driven** with Neon PostgreSQL support\n\nAll source files are well-structured with TypeScript, proper data-testid attributes for testing, and CSS-in-modules organization."}],"totalDurationMs":95185,"totalTokens":53837,"totalToolUseCount":28,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1911,"cache_read_input_tokens":47883,"output_tokens":4043,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1911},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
